	<!-- ============================================================
	     FrilCleanDoors  v1.2.2  -  shapes.xml
	
	     Makes player-crafted window shapes survive a hit or two
	     instead of shattering on the first contact, and lets you
	     upgrade them like any other shape.
	
	     How it works: window shape variants have three states - Full
	     (glass intact), Broken (cracked), Empty (frame only). Vanilla
	     gives the Full state MaterialHitpointMultiplier=0.001, which
	     on a weak-wood frame is 0.1 HP - any non-zero damage instantly
	     downgrades to Broken. This patch raises the multiplier to 0.1
	     so the Full state holds 10% of the material's MaxDamage before
	     downgrading. Broken and Empty states are left at vanilla.
	
	     Effective HP added by the Full state, by frame material:
	       frameShapes (weak wood, MaxDmg 100)  -> Full HP 10
	       woodShapes  (wood,      MaxDmg 500)  -> Full HP 50
	       concreteShapes / steelShapes         -> proportionally more
	
	     Total durability is ~10% above vanilla per window - enough
	     that the glass survives a hit or two, but small enough not
	     to significantly affect game balance.
	
	     v1.2.0: Full multi was 0.5 (50% break point, ~50% durability
	             inflation). Replaced with 0.1 in v1.2.1.
	     v1.2.2: removed the vanilla ItemCount=10000 upgrade trap so
	             windows can actually be upgraded (e.g. wood ->
	             cobblestone) like any other shape.
	
	     Bulletproof shapes use a separate shape group and a separate
	     block - they are NOT affected by this patch.
	
	     61 Full window shapes patched (multiplier).
	     59 Full window shapes patched (upgrade trap removed).
	     ============================================================ -->

